WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.850
- So we have time for one
last story to end this hour.

00:00:02.850 --> 00:00:03.874
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:03.874 --> 00:00:06.780
(upbeat music)

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.330
There's nothing worse at
a white elephant party

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:12.570
than when you've got the exact
gift you want in your hands

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:13.830
and some jerk takes it.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.560
They choose to take it
from you. That is not cool.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.170
That's how a Louisville dental
office treatment coordinator

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.360
was feeling when a colleague snatched up

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.210
her $25 T.J. Maxx gift
card out of her hands

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:25.860
during a holiday work gathering.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.170
But it turns out there
was nothing to fret about

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.750
because she ended up with
the best gift of the bunch.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.539
Just look at her reaction.

00:00:32.539 --> 00:00:35.372
(woman screaming)

00:00:37.935 --> 00:00:39.915
- That was my present.
- [Woman] Oh my God.

00:00:39.915 --> 00:00:42.119
- You can steal it three
times and I take it back.

00:00:42.119 --> 00:00:43.914
(audience cheering)

00:00:43.914 --> 00:00:46.230
- It has allowed her to do
great things for others.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.870
Everybody, we have her on the
line to explain everything.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.913
Say hi to Lori watching on WDIV-TV.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.240
What's up, Lori?

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:55.560
- Hi, Kelly. How are you?

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.970
- I am so good.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:59.820
Okay, so a colleague took your gift card,

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.380
but what did you end up with?

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:04.230
- She took my gift card
and I love T.J. Maxx,

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.620
but I ended up taking
some lottery tickets.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.290
In that, she gave me a lucky quarter

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:11.857
and all the girls in the
office started screaming,

00:01:11.857 --> 00:01:12.810
"Scratch them off!"

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:17.070
And so as I started scratching
all of those lottery tickets,

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:19.189
I actually hit on every one of them.

00:01:19.189 --> 00:01:20.490
It was amazing.

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:24.600
The last one was the $10 lottery ticket,

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:27.720
and as I scratched off the numbers first,

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.420
I already felt like this weird feeling.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.270
Two numbers, my number two and number 14.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:35.310
Number two is my husband's birthday,

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:37.590
and the 14th was when
my daughter was born.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.780
So as I started scratching off and seeing,

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:41.700
like the first one was 20,000,

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.820
the second one was 20,000,
I was like, "Oh my gosh."

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:46.910
In the second row, I won on all of my,

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:49.470
on the 14, on my daughter's birthday.

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:53.265
And that ticket ended
up winning me $175,000.

00:01:53.265 --> 00:01:54.113
(audience cheering)
- What in the?

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.310
I love your photo.
(laughs) That's amazing.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:02.760
So you're doing a lot more
with this money, right?

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:03.870
- I am.

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:06.120
When they asked me that first time,

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.670
I said I was gonna pay off
my daughter's student loans.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:11.490
But when you get home
and you think about it

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:14.100
and you pray about it, and
I looked over at my husband

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:16.590
and I said, "I've always
been so passionate

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:20.040
about working in dentistry
and I love Dr. Harmon."

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.190
And I decided that I was gonna open up

00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:27.600
a nonprofit organization
called "Smiles Once More".

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.750
It should be up and running in the spring.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.150
And I am hoping to change some lives

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.790
because not everyone has the ability

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:39.900
to be able to afford
dentistry, and they struggle.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:42.930
And your smile is everything.
It's how you get a job.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:44.910
It's, you know, who we are.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:49.061
And I just wanna be able to
help some people that need help.

00:02:49.061 --> 00:02:50.502
(audience clapping)

00:02:50.502 --> 00:02:51.840
- What a great person.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:53.910
I'm so glad you ended
up with those tickets.

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.530
Thank you so much, Lori.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:56.995
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:56.995 --> 00:02:59.156
- [Lori] Thank you.

00:02:59.156 --> 00:02:59.989
- And that's not all.

00:02:59.989 --> 00:03:02.700
Our season long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of Frixion,

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:04.560
the go-to erasable pen of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:05.580
want to celebrate those

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:07.740
selflessly helping others just like you.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.003
So they're gonna give you
$1,000. You won again.

00:03:10.003 --> 00:03:11.841
(audience cheering)
- Oh my God.

00:03:11.841 --> 00:03:13.560
Thank you so much.
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.080
- That means a lot.
- Thank you, Lori.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.310
And thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:21.360
Utkarsh Ambudkar, Kathleen
Madigan, Dr. Ian Saunders,

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:24.750
Mariana Hostway, Priscilla
Casper, Latoya Edwards,

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:25.673
and all our friends at NBC10 Boston.

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:29.650
Y'all have a great day and if
it's not, try and change it.

